.TH DEPLOY-SITE 1 "October 2026" "Noble Factor" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
Deploy-Site \- build the DevLore site and deploy it to its Azure Static Web App with the SWA CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B Deploy-Site
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Deploy-Site
installs the site's dependencies with
.BR "npm ci" ,
builds it with
.BR "npm run build" ,
and deploys
.I dist
to the Static Web App with the SWA CLI's
.BR "swa deploy" ,
by app name and resource group.
It runs
.B az login
first when Azure has no login.
It runs from the repository's root, wherever it is called from.
.PP
.BR Publish-Site (1)
is the usual way to publish; this one deploys by name rather than by deployment token.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show this manual page and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B AZURE_SWA_APP_NAME
The Static Web App. Default: devlore-noblefactor-com.
.TP
.B AZURE_RESOURCE_GROUP
Its resource group. Default: rg-devlore-site.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success \- the site is deployed.
.TP
.B 64
Usage error \- a missing or invalid option.
.TP
.B 69
A tool it needs is not on PATH.
.TP
.B 72
Critical file missing \- \fBDeclare-BashScript\fR is not on PATH; deploy the base layer, NobleFactor/noblefactor-engprod.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bin/Deploy-Site
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR Publish-Site (1),
.BR New-SiteHosting (1),
.BR az (1)
